# Keeps `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile from undoing the `npm ci` layer above
# it (docs/12-dev-workflow-ci.md §12.4). Without this, a host node_modules
# is copied straight over the freshly-installed one — which is both slower
# and wrong, since host installs can carry platform-specific binaries that
# don't run in the image.
#
# This matters more since worker/ arrived: it's a second npm package with
# its own ~300 MB of dependencies that the app image has no use for at all.
node_modules
worker/node_modules

# Cloudflare local state — a simulated D1 database and Miniflare's
# generated bundles. Local dev artifacts, never part of a build.
worker/.wrangler
worker/.dev.vars

# Expo/Metro build output and caches.
.expo
.expo-shared
dist
web-build

# Secrets and local config must never reach an image layer.
.env
.env.*

.git
.github
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Docs and scratch files the running app doesn't need.
*.md
!README.md
